 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asymmetry Assistant Curator Fellowship 2027-2029 at Notti
 ngham Contemporary
DESCRIPTION:Asymmetry Art Foundation and Nottingham Contemporary offer a fu
 lly funded two-year Assistant Curator Fellowship embedded in the curatoria
 l team of one of Europe's leading contemporary art institutions.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Asymmetry Art Foundation\, with Nottingham Contemporary\nLocation:
  Nottingham Contemporary\, Nottingham\, UK. Open internationally to early-
 career curators who identify with Chinese or Sinophone cultures or backgro
 unds\; visa and relocation support provided.\nAward: Annual salary of GBP 
 27\,556 for two years\, plus pension and National Insurance contributions\
 , annual leave in line with organisational policy plus UK bank holidays\, 
 visa and legal fee assistance where required\, and a travel and relocation
  allowance. No application fee.\nDuration: Two years\, 6 April 2027 to 5 A
 pril 2029.\n\nMore: https://www.asymmetryart.org/fellowships/open-calls/20
 27-asymmetry-assistant-curator-fellowship-nottingham-contemporary-opencall
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asymmetryart.org/fellowships/open-calls/2027-asymmetry-assi
 stant-curator-fellowship-nottingham-contemporary-opencall?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nottingham Contemporary\, Nottingham\, UK. Open internationally to
  early-career curators who identify with Chinese or Sinophone cultures or 
 backgrounds\; visa and relocation support provided.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ucla-meap-modern-endangered-archives-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART:20261117T072900Z
DTEND:20261117T075900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 PST: UCLA Modern Endangered Archives Program (MEAP):
  2026-27 Call for Applications
DESCRIPTION:Closes 16 Nov 2026 at 23:59 PST.\n\nThe UCLA Library Modern End
 angered Archives Program (MEAP)\, funded by Arcadia\, grants its ninth coh
 ort of awards to preserve\, document and digitize cultural heritage collec
 tions at risk from environmental conditions\, political uncertainty\, inhe
 rently unsustainable media\, inappropriate storage\, or communal and socia
 l change.\n\nOrganisation: UCLA Library\, Modern Endangered Archives Progr
 am\nLocation: Worldwide. Projects digitize at-risk collections where they 
 are held\; digitized materials are published open access in the UCLA Libra
 ry Digital Collections.\nAward: Planning Grants up to USD 20\,000 (up to 1
  year) for collection evaluation\, survey and inventory work before digiti
 zation. Project Grants up to USD 70\,000 (up to 2 years) for digitization 
 and metadata creation on well-organized collections\, or curation of exist
 ing digital assets. Regional Grants up to USD 100\,000 (up to 2 years) for
  digital collections drawing on three or more institutions\, families or r
 epositories around one theme\, hosted by an organization with prior MEAP e
 xperience. A separate AV Grants track (up to USD 100\,000\, for audio\, vi
 deo and film) opens in April 2027. No application fee.\nDuration: Planning
  Grants up to 1 year\; Project and Regional Grants up to 2 years\n\nMore: 
 https://meap.library.ucla.edu/call-for-applications/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://meap.library.ucla.edu/call-for-applications/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide. Projects digitize at-risk collections where they are he
 ld\; digitized materials are published open access in the UCLA Library Dig
 ital Collections.
END:VEVENT
